{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a destination that posts each batch it receives as the requests its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" splits it into: one request for an endpoint without limits. Each body is whatever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the encoder writes for its records, so events need no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance and the wire format is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"yours. It sends with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by default, or through any "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" you pass."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A send that gets no response, or a 5xx, 408 or 429 status, is sent again after the next wait of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": 1 second, doubling up to 60 seconds, unless you pass another. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination takes the next batch only once this one is delivered or dropped, so a tracker’s store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps the batch’s records until then. A batch the endpoint answers with any other status, whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request can never be sent, or that the encoder can’t encode is dropped, logged and reported on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", as is each record the encoder leaves out"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of its requests."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The tracing instrument injects the trace context of each request’s first record into its header","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fields, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is always the encoder’s.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach for this module to send to a server whose format you write yourself. For TraffluentCollector’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format, give the destination a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for PostHog,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"make it with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.postHog(projectToken:host:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"). To read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events inside the app or in a test, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InMemoryDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destinations"},{"type":"text","text":") instead."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","","struct PlansEncoder: BatchEncoder {","    func requests(for batch: [EventRecord]) -> BatchRequests<Never> {","        let plans = batch.compactMap { ($0.event as? SignedUp)?.plan }","        let body = EncodedBatch(body: Data(plans.joined(separator: \"\\n\").utf8), contentType: \"text\/plain\")","        return BatchRequests(requests: [EncodedRequest(body: body, recordIDs: batch.map(\\.id))], skippedRecords: [])","    }","}","","let server = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: endpointURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder(),","    backoff: try ExponentialBackoff(initialDelay: .seconds(2), maximumDelay: .seconds(120)))","let drops = server.dropReports","let watching = Task {","    for await drop in drops {","        print(\"Dropped a batch: \\(drop)\")","    }","}","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: server)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers this destination beside the others, and what a delivery does while a batch is retried."}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations"]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"HTTPDestinations","modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"externalID":"HTTPDestinations"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Sending batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/